            "title": "Strategy and bitcoin-buying firms face wider exclusion from stock indexes",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Michael Saylor's Strategy could soon be dropped from MSCI and potentially other major stock indexes, which analysts say could cost the bitcoin-hoarding giant up to $9 billion in demand for its shares and hurt the wider appeal of the sector.  After queries \u200bfrom clients, MSCI in October proposed ditching from its global benchmarks companies whose digital asset holdings represent 50% or more of their total assets. \u200cIt says they resemble investment funds, which it does not include in its benchmarks.  Shares in Strategy, which began life as software firm MicroStrategy, skyrocketed 3,000% after it began buying bitcoin in 2020, although they have since fallen sharply, and are down about 43% this year amid the cryptocurrency's slump.",
